WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:16.834
Henry stared at the stranger in surprise.

2
00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:21.240
"Yes, we're The Lemonade Detectives," he told him.

3
00:00:21.241 --> 00:00:25.289
"What do you mean, your ice-cream flavor was stolen?"

4
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:32.368
"I mean someone stole it!" the man exclaimed with a scowl. Then he sighed.

5
00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.417
"Sorry, I didn't mean to snap at you," he said in a calmer voice.

6
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:38.306
"I'm just upset."

7
00:00:38.307 --> 00:00:43.174
"Maybe we can help," Maggie said. "Tell us more about the case."

8
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:49.035
"My name is Mr. Tate. I'm getting ready to open a new business called the Dessert Den."

9
00:00:49.036 --> 00:00:54.604
"The Dessert Den?" Cole licked his lips. "Sounds delicious!"

10
00:00:54.605 --> 00:00:58.418
Henry thought the name of Mr. Tate's business sounded familiar.

11
00:00:58.419 --> 00:01:00.327
Then he remembered why.

12
00:01:00.328 --> 00:01:04.989
"The Dessert Den is in West Belltown, right?" he asked.

13
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:07.755
Mr. Tate nodded. "That's right."

14
00:01:07.756 --> 00:01:11.372
"How did you know that?" Maggie asked Henry.

15
00:01:11.373 --> 00:01:16.738
"My dad has been writing a series of stories about that part of town," Henry said.

16
00:01:16.739 --> 00:01:21.964
"There was a bad fire there a long time ago, and the neighborhood got run down.

17
00:01:21.965 --> 00:01:27.223
Now the town council wants to fix up the area and help new businesses open up."

18
00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:29.896
"I know where you mean," Cole said.

19
00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:33.268
"A lot of West Belltown is just empty lots now.

20
00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:36.139
Some guys from my soccer team live there."

21
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:43.576
Henry nodded. "Dad says the people who live in West Belltown have been using the empty lots for all sorts of things.

22
00:01:43.577 --> 00:01:48.940
They hold neighborhood barbecues there and play soccer and kickball, stuff like that."

23
00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:52.584
Mr. Tate cleared his throat loudly, looking impatient.

24
00:01:52.585 --> 00:01:57.135
"You kids are younger than I expected. Are you really detectives?"

25
00:01:57.136 --> 00:02:01.762
"Yes," Maggie said. "We've solved lots of mysteries.

26
00:02:01.763 --> 00:02:06.702
If anyone in Belltown can solve your case, it's The Lemonade Detectives!"

27
00:02:06.703 --> 00:02:10.274
"Okay." Mr. Tate still looked uncertain.

28
00:02:10.275 --> 00:02:12.721
"But I need this problem solved quickly.

29
00:02:12.722 --> 00:02:15.840
The Dessert Den's grand opening is this Friday."

30
00:02:15.841 --> 00:02:20.135
"Friday?" Cole cried. "That's tomorrow!"

31
00:02:20.136 --> 00:02:24.377
"But don't worry, we can do it," Maggie said quickly.

32
00:02:24.378 --> 00:02:27.075
"We've never failed to solve a case."

33
00:02:27.076 --> 00:02:29.604
There was a sudden shout from nearby.

34
00:02:29.605 --> 00:02:32.778
Henry saw a group of kids rushing toward them.

35
00:02:32.779 --> 00:02:36.085
Several of the kids were carrying baseball gloves or bats.

36
00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:38.642
All of them looked sweaty and tired.

37
00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:43.982
"Here come some customers," he told his friends. "They look thirsty."

38
00:02:43.983 --> 00:02:47.083
"Excuse us," Maggie told Mr. Tate.

39
00:02:47.084 --> 00:02:51.820
"As soon as we take care of these lemonade customers, we can talk more about your case."

40
00:02:51.821 --> 00:02:54.126
Mr. Tate checked his watch.

41
00:02:54.127 --> 00:02:57.578
"I'm meeting a plumber at the Dessert Den in a little while.

42
00:02:57.579 --> 00:03:01.396
There's a lot of last-minute work to do before the grand opening.

43
00:03:01.397 --> 00:03:06.078
Why don't you come over to the shop when you're finished here?"

44
00:03:06.079 --> 00:03:09.878
He hurried away before The Lemonade Detectives could answer.

45
00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:13.488
By then the baseball players had reached the lemonade stand.

46
00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:16.249
One of them was Henry's friend Nathan.

47
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.414
"One lemonade, please," Nathan said.

48
00:03:19.415 --> 00:03:23.241
Henry and his friends poured lemonade for all the kids.

49
00:03:23.242 --> 00:03:29.135
Most of them left after they got their lemonade, but Nathan sat down on the grass to drink his.

50
00:03:29.136 --> 00:03:33.528
"We'd better get over to the Dessert Den," Cole told Henry and Maggie.

51
00:03:33.529 --> 00:03:36.700
"Mr. Tate needs us to solve this case fast."

52
00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:43.305
"We can't all go," Maggie said. "Somebody has to stay here to sell lemonade."

53
00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:48.758
"Okay," Cole said. "You stay here, and Henry and I will go talk to Mr. Tate."

54
00:03:48.759 --> 00:03:51.502
"No way!" Maggie complained.

55
00:03:51.503 --> 00:03:54.392
"I stayed while you two went to get ice cream, remember?

56
00:03:54.393 --> 00:03:56.637
It's somebody else's turn."

57
00:03:56.638 --> 00:04:02.431
She looked stubborn. So did Cole. Henry thought fast.

58
00:04:02.432 --> 00:04:06.420
"Hey, Nathan," he said. "Want to sell lemonade for us?

59
00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:09.002
You can keep half of our profits."

60
00:04:09.003 --> 00:04:11.589
"Sure!" Nathan said.

61
00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.164
"What?" Maggie squawked.

62
00:04:14.165 --> 00:04:21.060
Henry shrugged. "If you don't like my idea, you can stay instead," he told his cousin.

63
00:04:21.061 --> 00:04:25.253
Maggie scowled. But finally she agreed to the plan.

64
00:04:25.254 --> 00:04:31.019
"Let's take our bikes," Cole suggested. "West Belltown is pretty far away.

65
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:38.598
It's too hot to walk there today."

66
00:04:38.599 --> 00:04:43.132
Once they reached West Belltown, they spotted the Dessert Den right away.

67
00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:46.605
It was the only finished building on the main avenue.

68
00:04:46.606 --> 00:04:51.005
The area around the Dessert Den was mostly covered in grass and weeds.

69
00:04:51.006 --> 00:04:54.632
Some kids were playing kickball in one of the grassy lots.

70
00:04:54.633 --> 00:05:01.207
"Look, there's my friend Emma," Maggie said. She waved and stopped her bike.

71
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:07.782
Emma and the other kids hurried over. Henry knew all of them from school.

72
00:05:07.783 --> 00:05:12.483
"What are you guys doing in West Belltown?" asked a kid named Robby.

73
00:05:12.484 --> 00:05:15.337
He was a year older than Henry and Cole.

74
00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:21.015
"The guy who owns the Dessert Den wants to hire us to solve a mystery," Maggie blurted out.

75
00:05:21.016 --> 00:05:23.626
Henry shot his cousin a warning look.

76
00:05:23.627 --> 00:05:27.706
Detectives had to be careful when they were talking about their cases.

77
00:05:27.707 --> 00:05:31.528
Robby's smile instantly turned into an angry scowl.

78
00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:35.331
"Why would you want to help him? Nobody wants him here!

79
00:05:35.332 --> 00:05:41.553
He should go back to wherever he came from and leave West Belltown alone!"
